  "details": "The Steadycam currently smooths out the rotation of all movements including teleports.\n\nThis can cause a dizzying effect to occur when a teleport rotates the player like when Respawning.\n\nCreate an option, or just as is, to have the Steadycam jump to the current view angle when a teleport occurs. It would be especially nice if it respected the Lerp On Remote flag for teleports. Where it only creates a discontinuity when a teleport with that flag disabled occurs.\n\nExample:\n\nIn Super VR Ball, the Steadycam should smooth out the rotation while on the ball since teleporting is using Lerp On Remote. However, when a new level starts or upon respawning the Steadycam should jump to the current rotation since that was a teleport with that flag disabled.",
